{"title":"Chemistry","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Overview\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Overview</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Organic_Chemistry\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Organic Chemistry</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Stoichiometry\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Stoichiometry</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Overview\">Overview</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Chemistry&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Overview\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><b>Chemistry</b> is the study of interactions between <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Atom\" title=\"Atom\">atoms</a> at a macroscopic or microscopic (molecular) level.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Organic_Chemistry\">Organic Chemistry</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Chemistry&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Organic Chemistry\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Organic chemistry is a branch of chemistry that focuses on molecules that contain carbon. Although most of organic chemistry is nonliving, organic chemistry is the basis of life.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Stoichiometry\">Stoichiometry</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Chemistry&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Stoichiometry\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Stoichiometry is about calculating the amount of certain substances in a chemical reaction.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Chemistry&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Chemistry&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018080301\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.009 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.013 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 18/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 268/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.313      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.313      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3808:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018080301 and revision id 277817. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}